    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Description\n\nI want to use `gc` for commenting in normal mode and `C` for comment in visual mode. I think the only way to do this now is to disable the automatic mapping through the config and then mapping it myself. \r\n\r\nCould you make it so if `mappings.visual_comment` is given through setup the it is used for the visual mode mapping. For backwards compatibility if its not given then `mappings.comment` is used. ",
